        <definition>static s32 XAsu_PlExtValidateKeyObjectParams</definition>
        <argsstring>(const XAsu_AesKeyObject *KeyObjectPtr)</argsstring>
        <name>XAsu_PlExtValidateKeyObjectParams</name>
        <param>
          <type>const <ref refid="struct_x_asu___aes_key_object" kindref="compound">XAsu_AesKeyObject</ref> *</type>
          <declname>KeyObjectPtr</declname>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>This function validates the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___aes_key_object" kindref="compound">XAsu_AesKeyObject</ref> structure parameters. </para>        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>KeyObjectPtr</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Pointer to the <ref refid="struct_x_asu___aes_key_object" kindref="compound">XAsu_AesKeyObject</ref> structure which holds the key object parameters.</para></parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para><itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>XST_SUCCESS, if validation of key object parameters is successful.</para></listitem><listitem><para>XASU_INVALID_ARGUMENT, if any argument is invalid. </para></listitem></itemizedlist>
</para></simplesect>
</para>        </detaileddescription>
        <inbodydescription>
<para>Validate that the key is provided from user memory.</para><para>Validate the key size and the key source supported by the PL crypto block. </para>        </inbodydescription>
